		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Driving Licence:</strong> Your driving licence is mandatory as it proves your identity and authorizes you to operate the vehicle.</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Vehicle Ownership Document:</strong> This document confirms your ownership of the vehicle and may include the Vehicle Registration Certificate (VRC) or the All India Permit (AIP).</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Repair and Service Records:</strong> Providing details of any repairs or services done to the vehicle can help ensure a smooth transportation process and may be required by the carrier company.</span></li>
	</ul>
	<p>By ensuring you have all the necessary documents, including the essential ones mentioned above, you can ensure a hassle-free car transportation in Patratu.</p>
	<p>Make sure to verify the credentials and reputation of the car carrier company you choose to ensure a reliable transportation service.</p>
	<p>Additionally, it is advisable to inspect your car before and after transportation to ensure that no damage has occurred during the journey.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



